+risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint
+R1,storage/data durability,"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer","Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments","Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures","Platform plus service owner"
+R2,audit behavior,"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table","No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis","Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior","Service owner"
+R3,configuration/runtime environment,"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly","Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory","Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup","Service owner"
+R4,API input validation,"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present","Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures","Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses","API owner"
+R5,HTTP integration contract,"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency","Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap","Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test","Service owner"
